<div class="mk-crumbbar"><div class="mk-wrap in"><a href="/markets">Markets</a><span class="sep">&rsaquo;</span><span class="here">Data Centers</span></div></div><section class="mk-hero" data-hana-bg="flow" data-variant="light" data-fade="none"><div class="mk-wrap mk-hero-in"><div><div class="mk-eyebrow">Markets we serve</div><h1 class="mk-h1">Precision EMS for AI data center infrastructure</h1><p class="mk-lede">Hana works where signal integrity meets thermal performance in the AI data center: the control electronics and modules around thermoelectric cooling devices, and the high-density boards inside the optical test equipment used to qualify high-speed transceiver hardware.</p><div class="mk-btns"><a href="/contact" class="hana-btn hana-btn-primary" style="padding:12px 22px;font-size:12px;">Talk to us <i data-lucide="arrow-right" style="width:14px;height:14px;margin-left:6px;"></i></a><a href="#products" class="hana-btn hana-btn-secondary" style="padding:12px 22px;font-size:12px;">Our scope</a></div></div><div class="mk-hero-media"><div class="mk-ph" style="aspect-ratio:auto;height:420px;border-bottom:0;"><div style="position:absolute;top:10px;left:12px;width:18px;height:18px;opacity:.4;z-index:1;"><svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="var(--hana-blue)" stroke-width="1.5"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 3v4M12 17v4M3 12h4M17 12h4"></path></svg></div><span class="cap">[ Data Centers &mdash; photography needed ]</span></div></div></div><div class="mk-wrap" style="position:relative;z-index:1;padding-bottom:52px;"><div class="mk-strip"><span class="hana-spec-label" style="flex-shrink:0;">Product examples</span><div class="mk-chips"><span>Thermoelectric coolers (TEC)</span><span>Optical transceiver test systems</span><span>SiC power conversion</span><span>High density PCBA</span></div></div></div></section><section class="mk-dark"><div class="mk-wrap in"><div style="max-width:760px;margin-bottom:34px;"><div class="mk-eyebrow on-dark">Why AI-infrastructure buyers choose Hana</div><h2 class="mk-h2 on-dark">Built for the precision edge of AI infrastructure</h2><p class="mk-body on-dark" style="margin:14px 0 0;">AI infrastructure pushes two different kinds of precision onto its supply chain, and Hana works at both. The first is thermal: the driver, power-management and current-regulation electronics around thermoelectric cooling (TEC) devices, and the modules that integrate them — the layer closest to the heat source in optical transceivers, co-packaged optics and memory stacks. The second is board density: the high-density PCBAs inside optical test equipment, where component count and routing density leave little margin and the joints that matter sit hidden beneath the packages. Both call for fine-pitch placement, controlled reflow and inspection coverage rather than sampling.</p></div><div class="mk-points"><div class="pt"><div class="t">Combined PCBA + OSAT under one roof</div><p>The board and the integrated circuit can be qualified together inside one supplier, shortening qualification cycles for precision programs.</p></div><div class="pt"><div class="t">High-density board assembly</div><p>Fine-pitch placement, high layer counts and dense routing, with the inspection and test coverage these boards require — the assembly discipline behind both strands.</p></div><div class="pt"><div class="t">In-house automation engineering</div><p>Programs here run on lines designed and built by Hana's own engineers, per program rather than retrofitted from shared capacity.</p></div></div></div></section><section id="products" data-hana-bg="pcb" data-variant="light" data-fade="none" style="background:#fff;border-top:1px solid var(--line);position:relative;overflow:hidden;"><div class="mk-wrap" style="position:relative;z-index:1;padding-top:64px;padding-bottom:60px;"><div style="max-width:700px;margin-bottom:26px;"><h2 class="mk-h2">Our scope</h2><p class="mk-body">Three strands of work reach the AI data center: the control electronics around thermoelectric cooling devices, high-density PCBA for high-speed oscilloscopes, and SiC power conversion assembly.</p></div><div class="mk-spoke-main"><div class="mk-sheet"><div class="row"><div class="lab"><span class="n">01</span><span class="t">Thermoelectric cooling (TEC) electronics</span></div><div class="desc"><p>Thermoelectric cooling is solid-state — no compressor, no refrigerant, no moving parts. A TEC sits directly against the component it cools and can be adjusted in milliseconds, so it holds one small, specific area at a set temperature rather than cooling a whole enclosure. It works alongside heat sinks and liquid cold plates rather than replacing them.</p><p>In AI infrastructure this matters wherever heat and signal integrity meet — GPU and high-bandwidth memory hotspots, co-packaged optics, pluggable optical transceivers and switch ASICs, where thermal drift becomes throttling or signal loss.</p></div></div><div class="row"><div class="lab"><span class="n">02</span><span class="t">High-density PCBA for high-speed oscilloscopes</span></div><div class="desc"><p>Dense, multi-layer boards for the high-speed oscilloscopes used to qualify optical transceiver hardware, assembled on fine-pitch SMT lines with X-ray on the joints a dense layout hides. They form the backbone of signal qualification by hyper-scaler end customers.</p></div></div><div class="row"><div class="lab"><span class="n">03</span><span class="t">SiC power conversion</span></div><div class="desc"><p>Data-center power distribution is moving toward solid-state conversion — silicon carbide switching with a high-frequency magnetic stage in place of an iron-core transformer — which turns the power stage from a passive component into an assembled electronic one. That assembly is work Hana already runs for automotive and industrial power management devices: SiC die onto ceramic substrate, interconnect sized to the current the design carries, and the drive electronics built around it.</p></div></div></div></div></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--hana-blue-tint);border-top:1px solid var(--line);border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);"><div class="mk-wrap" style="padding-top:56px;padding-bottom:56px;"><div style="max-width:720px;margin-bottom:24px;"><div class="mk-eyebrow">Footprint</div><h2 class="mk-h2 sm">Where we build</h2></div><div class="mk-locs"><a class="mk-loc" href="/locations/lamphun"><span class="co"><i data-lucide="map-pin" style="width:13px;height:13px;color:var(--hana-blue);"></i><span class="hana-spec-label">Thailand</span></span><div class="nm">Lamphun</div><div class="note">TEC control-electronics PCBA, high-density PCBA &amp; module assembly</div><span class="cta">View plant <i data-lucide="arrow-right" style="width:12px;height:12px;"></i></span></a></div></div></section><section style="background:#fff;"><div class="mk-wrap" style="padding-top:56px;padding-bottom:60px;"><div style="max-width:700px;margin-bottom:22px;"><div class="mk-eyebrow">FAQ</div><h2 class="mk-h2 sm">Frequently asked questions</h2><p class="mk-body">Common questions from AI-infrastructure engineering and procurement teams.</p></div><div style="max-width:860px;"><details class="mk-faq" open><summary><span class="mk-faq-mk"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"></path></svg></span><span style="flex:1;">What does Hana build for data centers?</span></summary><p class="mk-faq-a">Two things: the control electronics and integrated modules around thermoelectric cooling (TEC) devices, and high-density PCBA for the high-speed oscilloscopes used to qualify optical transceiver hardware.</p></details><details class="mk-faq"><summary><span class="mk-faq-mk"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"></path></svg></span><span style="flex:1;">What does Hana build for high-speed oscilloscopes?</span></summary><p class="mk-faq-a">High-density PCBAs for the oscilloscopes used to test high-speed optical transceivers — dense, multi-layer boards assembled on fine-pitch SMT lines with X-ray inspection on the joints a dense layout hides.</p></details><details class="mk-faq"><summary><span class="mk-faq-mk"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"></path></svg></span><span style="flex:1;">What is thermoelectric cooling (TEC) in an AI data center?</span></summary><p class="mk-faq-a">TEC is a solid-state precision-cooling layer placed closest to the heat source. It does not replace heat sinks or liquid cold plates — it works alongside them, regulating temperature where signal integrity or chip performance is most sensitive.</p></details><details class="mk-faq"><summary><span class="mk-faq-mk"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"></path></svg></span><span style="flex:1;">Where does Hana manufacture this work?</span></summary><p class="mk-faq-a">From our Lamphun PCBA facility in Northern Thailand, with dedicated automation lines built per program by our in-house engineering team.</p></details><details class="mk-faq"><summary><span class="mk-faq-mk"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"></path></svg></span><span style="flex:1;">Can Hana scale a new data-center program?</span></summary><p class="mk-faq-a">Yes — through a measured, milestone-driven ramp from qualification to low-volume manufacturing to scale, with dedicated lines rather than shared capacity.</p></details></div></div></section><section class="mk-cta" data-hana-bg="flow" data-variant="dark" data-fade="none"><div class="mk-wrap in"><div><h2 class="mk-h2 on-dark" style="max-width:520px;">Start an AI data-center program with Hana</h2><p class="mk-body on-dark" style="font-size:16px;max-width:480px;">Working on an AI thermal-management, high-speed optical or high-density board program that needs a precision EMS partner? Tell us what the product does — our Thailand team handles inquiries directly.</p></div><div class="acts"><a href="/contact" class="hana-btn hana-btn-on-dark" style="padding:12px 22px;font-size:12px;">Contact us <i data-lucide="arrow-right" style="width:14px;height:14px;margin-left:6px;"></i></a></div></div></section>
